Id: dev004w
Severity: WARN
Category: filesystem
Check: check_devices
Fix: Restrict it with a udev rule or group ownership if it need not be world readable.
References: udev(7)
Controls: CIS 3.3; NIST AC-3; ISO 8.3; CE Secure configuration

The device can be read by any user. For most devices that is harmless
and intended, but a few leak information: /dev/kmsg is the kernel log,
which may show hardware, drivers and addresses an attacker would find
useful (setting kernel.dmesg_restrict=1 only governs the dmesg call, not
this file). Review whether the device needs to be world readable and
restrict it with udev rules or group ownership if not.
